# Identity + auth enforcement

Phase 4 + Phase 6 of the multi-tenant rollout. Hard rules 27 + 31
(see [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md)) plus the Phase 4 enforcement layer.

## Backend

- Every API route MUST be protected by either:
  - `Depends(require_authenticated)` on a single route, OR
  - `dependencies=[Depends(require_authenticated)]` at the router
    level via [`secure_router`](mdc:aqp/api/security.py), OR
  - a more specific dep like `require_scope("data:write")` or
    `require_membership("editor", "workspace")`.
- The bypass allowlist is :data:`PUBLIC_ROUTERS` in
  [`aqp/api/security.py`](mdc:aqp/api/security.py) — new public
  endpoints require an explicit code-review note explaining why.
- Enforcement mode is gated by ``AQP_AUTH_ENFORCE=strict|permissive``.
  Permissive logs the violation + tags the OTEL span without
  blocking; flip to ``strict`` once the dashboard shows zero
  would-be denies for 24 h.
- Scopes are derived from the JWT in this priority order: OAuth
  ``scope`` string -> Auth0 ``permissions`` array -> AQP-namespaced
  ``https://aqp/scopes`` array -> ``https://aqp/roles`` array
  (expanded via the role lattice in
  [`aqp.config.defaults`](mdc:aqp/config/defaults.py)).
- Custom-claim namespace is :attr:`Settings.auth_claims_namespace`
  (default ``https://aqp/``). See
  [docs/auth0-actions.md](mdc:docs/auth0-actions.md) for the
  Action snippet.

## Lazy provisioning

- First OIDC login routes through
  [`provision_user_from_claims`](mdc:aqp/auth/user.py). The Phase 4
  extension also reads the AQP-namespaced ``org_id`` / ``team_id`` /
  ``workspace_id`` / ``roles`` custom claims and upserts matching
  [`Membership`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_tenancy.py) rows
  idempotently.
- The Auth0 Action calls
  [`/_internal/auth0/sync`](mdc:aqp/api/routes/auth0_sync.py) on
  every login. The endpoint is M2M-only (Bearer token signed by the
  same tenant) and returns the custom claims the Action injects.

## Frontend

- ``useAuth`` ([`frontend/src/lib/auth/useAuth.ts`](mdc:frontend/src/lib/auth/useAuth.ts))
  returns the user + ``claims`` (orgId / teamId / workspaceId /
  roles[]) derived from the access token.
- ``useClaimsToTenancy`` hydrates the Zustand tenancy store from
  those claims on the first render after login.
- The Phase 6 ``ContextBar`` ([`frontend/src/components/shell/ContextBar.tsx`](mdc:frontend/src/components/shell/ContextBar.tsx))
  exposes EntityPickers for org / team / workspace / project / lab
  so users can pin context manually.

## Don't list

- Don't read ``settings.<service>_client_*`` for OIDC credentials —
  use [`CredentialResolver`](mdc:aqp/credentials/resolver.py).
- Don't hit ``*.well-known/openid-configuration`` directly — go
  through the active
  [`IdentityProvider`](mdc:aqp/auth/providers/protocol.py).
- Don't add a new route without an auth dep unless it's on the
  :data:`PUBLIC_ROUTERS` allowlist. The Phase 4 sweep will catch
  violations once we flip to ``strict``.
- Don't accept ``actor`` / ``workspace_id`` / ``project_id`` from
  the request body on the MCP HTTP server — override with the
  values from the verified JWT + tenancy headers (see
  [`build_mcp_router`](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/server.py)).

